{
  "id": 402541588,
  "iid": 20665,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "XML: Defer field registration",
  "description": "Parse the processing instructions of the DTDs (and the initial doc type\ndeclaration and first element) with libxml2, which is much faster than\nthe flex based parser. Get enough information to register media types\nand protocols as needed, and then defer actual field registration until\nlater. (The media type registration must happen so that handoffs are\ncorrect; similarly the protocols have to be registered with their\nprefixes.) The full field registration still requires the flex based parser,\nat least for now, because libxml2 and other APIs don't make it easy to\nget information out of a DTD in the structure we want (as opposed to\nusing a DTD for validation.)\n\nThe flex-based parser also supports both files that contain standalone\nexternal DTDs, and files with a structure that resembles an XML document\nwith an internal DTD, but no actual XML tags (and thus not a valid\nXML document.) Continue to handle both types.\n\nThis speeds up initialization, because reading the files with flex\nwas a significant part of startup.\n\nPing #20508",
